---
const SIGNUP_URL = 'https://go.marginapp.in';
const tags = ['What-if price', 'Reference ratios', 'Fill down a row', 'Notes on a valuation', 'Filter by list', 'Search by name'];
---

<section class="py-24 lg:py-32 overflow-hidden">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-16 items-center">
      <div class="reveal lg:order-2">
        <p class="text-xs text-gold-400 tracking-widest uppercase mb-4">DCF Valuation</p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl font-light text-cream leading-tight mb-6">
          Project earnings forward,<br />
          <em class="font-semibold not-italic">find the fair value</em>
        </h2>
        <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed mb-6">
          DCF in Margin lets you build a full financial model, projecting revenue growth, operating
          margins, depreciation, tax, capex and working capital year by year. Discount the resulting
          free cash flows back to today for an intrinsic value, and read it against the market price
          to decide whether the stock is worth buying, holding, or leaving alone.
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed mb-6">
          The grid is built for the way the work actually goes. Fill a ratio down the projection years
          with a drift per year in basis points rather than typing each cell. Keep your own reference
          ratios beside the model, so the multiple or margin you judge a business by is on screen while
          you set the assumption. Attach a note to the valuation recording what you were underwriting
          and why.
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed mb-8">
          A what-if price lets you override the quote, by an amount or by a percentage, and watch
          enterprise value, market cap and the summary move with it, without that price being saved
          into the valuation. Every valuation stays anchored to the quarter it was valued for, so a
          number you look at a year later still tells you what it was built on.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-8">
          {tags.map((tag) => (
            <span class="px-3 py-1 text-xs text-muted border border-border rounded-full">{tag}</span>
          ))}
        </div>
        <a
          href={SIGNUP_URL}
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-medium text-gold-400 hover:text-gold-300 transition-colors group"
        >
          Try DCF Valuation
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M13.5 4.5 21 12m0 0-7.5 7.5M21 12H3" />
          </svg>
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="reveal reveal-delay-2 lg:order-1">
        <div class="relative rounded-xl border border-border bg-navy-800/40 overflow-hidden">
          <div class="absolute inset-x-0 top-0 h-px bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent via-gold-400/30 to-transparent"></div>
          <div class="p-6">
            <p class="text-xs text-muted tracking-widest uppercase mb-6">DCF Model Inputs</p>
            <div class="space-y-3 mb-6">
              {[
                { label: 'Revenue Growth Rate', value: '18%', sub: 'Filled down, −50 bps a year' },
                { label: 'Operating Margin', value: '22%', sub: 'Stabilising assumption' },
                { label: 'Discount Rate', value: '12%', sub: 'Market cap ₹18,400 Cr' },
              ].map((row) => (
                <div class="flex items-center justify-between py-3 border-b border-border/50">
                  <div>
                    <p class="text-sm text-ink">{row.label}</p>
                    <p class="text-xs text-muted">{row.sub}</p>
                  </div>
                  <span class="font-display text-lg text-cream">{row.value}</span>
                </div>
              ))}
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-lg bg-navy-950/50 border border-border/60 p-4 mb-4">
              <p class="text-[11px] text-muted tracking-widest uppercase mb-3">Reference Ratios</p>
              <div class="space-y-1.5">
                {[
                  { name: 'Sector median P/E', value: '32' },
                  { name: 'Own 5-yr median EV/EBITDA', value: '18' },
                ].map((ratio) => (
                  <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between text-xs">
                    <span class="text-muted uppercase tracking-wide">{ratio.name}</span>
                    <span class="text-cream font-medium">{ratio.value}</span>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-lg bg-navy-950/60 border border-gold-400/20 p-5">
              <p class="text-xs text-muted mb-1">Intrinsic value per share, valued for Q1 FY 2026-27</p>
              <p class="font-display text-4xl font-semibold text-gold-400">₹1,840</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-2">Against the quoted ₹2,340, a 22% premium to fair value</p>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-4 flex items-start gap-2 text-xs text-muted">
              <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-amber-400 mt-1 shrink-0"></span>
              <span>What-if price ₹2,100 (−10.3%) is applied to the summary and is not saved with the valuation.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
